WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.120
Anime can get pretty gruesome.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.060
But what horrific shows are worth your time?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:09.040
Well, from tales of malevolent spirits to
portraits of people shattered into inhumanity,

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.460
these are most terrifying anime you can watch.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.420
Go Nagai's Devilman manga has been adapted
more than once, but 2018's Devilman Crybaby

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.360
might just be the most terrifying adaptation
of them all.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.580
Directed by Masaaki Yuasa, this version hews
closer to the manga than others and incorporates

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:30.739
Yuasa's trademark character focus, resulting
in a story as emotionally potent as it is

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:31.240
horrifying.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.080
Akira and Ryo, friends since childhood, are
the series' central figures.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.180
Ryo convinces Akira to become the titular
“Devilman” to fight off an ancient race

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:39.940
of demons.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.540
But all is not as it seems, and what unfolds
manages to shock Devilman newbies and diehard

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.550
fans alike.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.850
Death, disfigurement, violence, are all on
vivid display here.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.930
The series penultimate episode, Go to Hell,
You Mortals, is an absolute parade of grotesqueries,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:58.640
wherein beloved characters are mutilated,
killed, and reduced to desecrated body parts.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.240
But Devilman Crybaby's true nightmare is the
gulf that opens between Akira and Ryo, despite

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.600
their careful planning, best intentions, and
literally divine power.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.780
This isn't just a horror story about man's
inhumanity to man, but about the destruction

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.640
of love itself at the hands of selfishness
and cruelty.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.640
Horror isn't typically considered a beautiful
genre, but Mononoke is a gorgeous series by

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.880
anyone's estimation.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.400
Consisting of 12 episodes, Mononoke tells
the story of a nameless medicine seller who

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.860
hunts mononoke spirits across feudal Japan.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.280
Mononoke can't be easily slain, however.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.219
The medicine seller must first understand
the form they take, and why they took it,

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:34.649
before he can dispatch them.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:37.380
What results is an anime of uncommon psychological
depth.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:41.740
Human nature is the source of all the scares
in Mononoke, and as such, the lines between

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.539
good and bad are profoundly blurred.

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:48.149
The series’ visuals, which resemble 2D paper
cut-outs, intensify this horizontal approach

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:48.700
to horror.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.060
There's no locale that looks "normal," and
as such, terror creeps in with rare subtlety.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.039
Everything from ukiyo-e woodblocks to Art
Nouveau is incorporated into Mononoke's style,

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:02.460
and you can't help but marvel at its aesthetic
flourishes as a grisly scene unfolds.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.880
But that's the point of the anime.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:09.760
Serial Experiments Lain follows Lain Iwakura,
a 14-year-old girl living in suburban Japan,

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.099
who has her quiet life upended by an email
from a dead student.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:17.030
The student claims not to have actually died,
but instead abandoned her physical form to

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.180
live within "the Wired."

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.140
Over the course of 13 tense episodes, Lain
goes from introverted girlhood to outright

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.989
omnipotence, in a world where the boundary
between the material and the virtual has frayed

00:02:26.989 --> 00:02:27.640
to nothing.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:32.040
Serial Experiments Lain is, first and foremost,
a work of science fiction, but it commits

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.400
so wholeheartedly to exploring the possibilities
of artificial intelligence that it becomes

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.720
a work of profound horror.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.780
Reality, Lain argues, is a thing people agree
on, and if that consensus can be manipulated,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.040
reality will be altered.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.980
Lain and the audience alike are granted no
quarter as the anime delves into the nature

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.540
of a world ruled by inhuman intelligence whose
influence can't be stopped.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.740
Every time Lain sits at her desk, her slim
figure dwarfed by the reef of screens, the

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.060
viewer understands that the world is changing
in a way we aren't prepared for.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.840
Satoshi Kon's Perfect Blue is among the most
influential anime to ever exist.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.600
Madonna incorporated clips of it into her
2001 Drowned World tour.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.379
A Director Darren Aronofsky remade a scene
from Perfect Blue in Requiem for a Dream.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:13.909
Why this far-flung influence?

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:16.590
It’s simple; Perfect Blue is a masterpiece
of dread.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.740
Mima, our protagonist, has just left a pop
idol group to become a serious actress.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.579
But as threatening faxes pour in and a website
entitled "Mima's Room" — containing diary

00:03:25.579 --> 00:03:30.310
entries purportedly written by Mima herself
— gains momentum, Mima realizes not all

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.330
is as it seems.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:35.020
The events of Perfect Blue are themselves
horrific, but it's Kon's dizzying approach

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.040
to their portrayal that make Perfect Blue
the nightmare it is.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:42.840
Frantic cuts disorient the viewer, odd scene
changes mimic Mima's increasingly disordered

00:03:42.859 --> 00:03:46.920
mind, and mirrors, screens, and windows refract
a world that has lost its meaning.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.030
Mima descends into an underworld of illusion,
and the viewer has only her perspective to

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.939
rely on, one that draws into question the
reliability of reality.

00:03:54.939 --> 00:03:58.530
There's a culprit held to account at the end
of Perfect Blue, but their actions are only

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.670
part of the story.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.240
The real terror, in Mima's mind and the viewer's,
lies in her world's collapse.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:09.080
Corpse Party's long, bloody history began
in 1996, as a simple PC video game.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:14.340
Today, the Corpse Party franchise encompasses
manga spin-offs, live-action films, and drama

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:14.840
CDs.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.640
Corpse Party: Tortured Souls, is 2013's anime
adaptation of the beloved series.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.801
Years before the series' beginning, Heavenly
Host Elementary School was the site of a series

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.520
of brutal kidnappings and killings.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.460
Though it was razed, a new high school was
built in its place and filled with teenagers

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.210
who don't understand the malevolent psychic
energy that surrounds them, until they find

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.889
themselves trapped in a nightmare version
of Heavenly Host.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:39.470
Corpse Party is a brutal, bloody series that
revels in the macabre.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:43.240
It's got spilled innards, severed tongues,
and bifurcated bodies.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.560
If you can stomach this, it's a satisfyingly
savage tale of the past's long shadows and

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.280
the youth forced to grow up within them.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.160
The trauma they've inherited isn't their own,
but it’s their job to process it anyway.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.480
Shiki, which chronicles the destruction of
a small town by the inhuman monsters that

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.840
live in the mansion on the town's outskirts,
is a classic vampire story.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:05.389
The shiki are hypnotic, undying figures with
inhuman drives, as utterly unknowable as they

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:07.099
are eerily similar to everyday people.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.140
Those who are killed are reborn as shiki.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:13.260
Megumi, the first to die, goes from being
a small-town girl with big-city dreams to

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:16.090
being an undead killer with disdain for her
hometown.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:19.819
This might sound familiar, but what makes
Shiki a truly memorable work of horror is

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.360
the truth of the shiki themselves.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.780
At heart, the shiki just want to build a peaceful
home.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.780
The shiki's actions are vile, but the anime
never shies from the truth of their tragic

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:28.280
situation.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:32.300
They exist, they must feed, and they're trying
to find a way to do both with a minimum of

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:32.840
cruelty.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.680
The impossibility of reconciling these things
is what makes Shiki such a resonant horror

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.360
story.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:44.180
No Longer Human began as a 1948 novel by legendary
author Osamu Dazai, and it's a story as powerful

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.949
as it is challenging to adapt.

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:51.740
Yet 2009 saw that accomplished when Aoi Bungaku
a 12-episode anime series featuring adaptations

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.099
of popular Japanese literature devoted the
first four episodes of its run to animating

00:05:56.099 --> 00:05:57.099
No Longer Human.

00:05:57.099 --> 00:06:01.449
Though Aoi Bungaku takes liberties with its
source material, the core conceit remains

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:01.940
intact.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:06.740
Protagonist Yozo, feels completely detached
from everything that makes one genuinely human.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.750
Watching him disastrously fail to connect
is a truly harrowing and relatable portrait

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:11.830
of brokenness.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:16.160
His life might not be anything like the viewer's,
but as in the original novel, almost anyone

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.820
can see a little of themselves in Yozo.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.500
That's what No Longer Human forces us to view
through Yozo's inhumanity.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.060
In this, he's far more human than he realizes,
and that's the most terrifying thing of all.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:31.120
Years before the events of Another, a student
in Yomiyama Middle School suddenly died.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:35.030
Her classmates, reeling with grief, pretended
as though she hadn't died at all, to the point

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:36.960
of reserving her seat at graduation.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.160
This culminated in the deceased classmate's
mysterious appearance in the class's graduation

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:41.660
photo.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:46.160
Years later, a boy named Koichi begins his
time in the same class late, due to illness,

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.140
and he discovers that something is amiss.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.920
Misaki, a quiet classmate, is entirely ignored
by the other students.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.740
And then, one by one, Koichi's peers start
dying.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.940
Misaki is the only one who isn't surprised
by these tragedies, and only she understands

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.940
how to stop them.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.419
The anime's moments of violence, terror, and
dread make it the sort of nightmare any horror

00:07:04.419 --> 00:07:07.480
fan can enjoy, but their true power lies beyond
brief thrills.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.680
They're the pillars of the story's central
tragedy.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:14.060
The class is locked within a cycle of grief
that can only be broken by that most crucial

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.200
thing: acceptance.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.500
Their inability to do so is the series' truest
nightmare of all.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.300
To be young and in love.

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:24.560
Happy Sugar Life addresses the virtues of
this sublime state, only to confront the viewer

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:29.069
with the reality of its starring couple Satou,
a teenage girl with a hard-luck past, and

00:07:29.069 --> 00:07:32.500
Shio, the kind-hearted eight-year-old that
Satou keeps locked in her apartment.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:36.620
Satou will do anything to conceal and protect
the "happy sugar life" she believes she's

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.140
created for her and Shio.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:42.660
Theirs is a love of pristine purity, according
to Satou, and there's no evil she won't commit

00:07:42.669 --> 00:07:44.520
in her devotion to its preservation.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.430
Happy Sugar Life never glories in the details
of Satou's grisliest acts.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:52.520
This anime chills the viewer with a vision
of just how people can twist each other into

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.020
monsters.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.080
Satou, exposed to only the most dysfunctional
relationship models as a child, believes that

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.040
kidnapping a child is excusable in the name
of true love.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.540
But it is Shio's character arc that really
terrifies.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:07.140
Having known only abandonment and violence
so far in her short life, she can't recognize

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:11.620
Satou for the monster she is, nor identify
herself as an individual beyond what Satou

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:12.650
projects upon her.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:16.699
What results is a story about how entirely
people can destroy the ones they love and

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.540
just how invisible the process can be.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:25.120
An alternative ending to Neon Genesis Evangelion’s
controversial final episode, The End of Evangelion

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.340
shows us the apocalypse.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:31.300
NERV, the paramilitary group responsible for
the Evangelion units that our heroes pilot,

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.510
is being used by its commander, Gendo Ikari,
to hasten the end of the world.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.659
He succeeds, though not as he would've liked.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.060
Prickly Asuka is disemboweled.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:43.740
Quiet Rei attains Biblical power and joins
all of humanity into a single consciousness.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.140
Protagonist Shinji survives, yet the story
ends on a shot of him and Asuka alone in the

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:48.900
ruined world.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.380
It’s implied that humanity might reform,
but in that moment, Shinji attempts to strangle

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.380
Asuka to death.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.260
When he fails, Asuka mutters the last line
of the film,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.940
"Kimochi warui,"

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.240
which is most often translated as, "I feel
sick," or, "How disgusting."

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:10.080
The End of Evangelion is possibly about hope,
but mostly, it's about the venality of the

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.560
world, the corruption of the powerful, and
the inevitability of decay.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:19.040
Shadow Star Narutaru begins as a tale about
a pigtailed everygirl and her mysterious alien

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.330
friend, Hoshimaru.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:25.100
You might be thinking that this sounds like
Digimon or Cardcaptor Sakura, a story of youngsters

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.940
and their unlikely companions saving the world
with their supernatural bond.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.480
This is very much by design.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.540
Hoshimaru is adorable, Shiina is a cheery
charmer, and the opening theme features purposefully

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.620
childlike drawings of the cast alongside their
alien friends.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.910
It's sweet, it's bright, and it features a
lot of harmonica.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.540
Somehow, Shadow Star Narutaru begins this
way and then ends, 13 episodes later, as one

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.100
of the most graphically disturbing anime series
of the 2000s.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.600
Characters are beheaded, impaled, forced to
eat maggots, have their severed heads mounted

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:59.800
on dolls, and experience a whole host of other
grisly horrors too graphic to be described.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:03.970
Shadow Star Narutaru is, in the end, a series
that absolutely glories in the worst things

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.380
people can do to each other.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.980
Watching it is dizzying, as moments of grotesque
horror are often juxtaposed against scenes

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:14.060
of peaceful daily life, to say nothing of
Shiina, whose blue-haired perkiness becomes

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.620
more and more discordant as the series darkens.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.180
Its abrupt ending only makes the series more
upsetting.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.700
Shadow Star Narutaru charms, horrifies, and
then, somewhat inexplicably, ends.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:28.260
The viewer is left to absorb all that unfolded
on screen with little in the way of explanation

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.720
and definitely nothing resembling comfort.

